  "text": "In Mara’s earlier story, you guided Mara to ask permission, fetch tape and help repair the boy’s bird. The boy carried that same bird onto the dock.\n\nSix posts and two ropes are beside the repair box. Each rope runs along one side: near bank, center, far bank. The same ropes extend as you build.\n\nThe Torn Wing has been shared with the people here. Mara’s lantern keeps this contribution. You can choose its picture or keep the repair picture.\n\nThe show plays from beginning to end. Loop changes the pictures automatically. You can pause, replay, or open the complete text with reading help.\n\nRina puts the whole lump in the oven for the recipe’s baking time. The outside browns, but the middle is still doughy. She sets this batch aside.\n\nTheir bread stays here. This loaf is for Sol. I’ll come back to give the customers their orders, so I cannot stay at the garden gathering today.\n\nThis saved adventure keeps its original telling. Start a new adventure to play the expanded story; this one will be kept in your local archive.\n\nRina tried baking the whole lump for the recipe’s baking time. The outside browned while the middle stayed doughy, so she set that batch aside.\n\nSol brought his unfinished page. At the gathering, Pip helped him add an ending about what followed the repair, and Sol shared that part too.\n\nSol read A Small Repair and the ending he and Pip had prepared. The others listened to an account he had once thought too ordinary to bring.\n\nMara’s earlier dock: her office and tape on the left; the boy and his torn paper bird on the right. Named controls perform the same actions.\n\nWhen you ask for AI feedback, your answer and the relevant story text are sent to the AI service. Your story progress stays in this browser.",
